        "passage": "The Internet has changed our lives in many ways. We can use it to learn, work, shop, and communicate with friends.\n\nHowever, the Internet also brings some problems. Some students spend too much time playing online games. This is bad for their eyes and studies. Some people share too much personal information online, which can be dangerous.\n\nTo use the Internet safely, you should follow these rules: First, don't spend more than two hours online each day. Second, never share your real name, address, or phone number with strangers. Third, if someone says something bad to you online, tell your parents or teachers immediately.\n\nThe Internet is a useful tool, but we must use it wisely. Remember, the Internet is a tool, not your whole life. Go outside, talk to real people, and enjoy the real world!\n\n---\n\nSpring Festival is the most important traditional festival in China. It usually comes in January or February. Before Spring Festival, people clean their houses, buy new clothes, and prepare delicious food.\n\nOn Spring Festival Eve, families get together and have a big dinner. The most popular food is dumplings. In some places, people also eat fish, because the Chinese word for 'fish' sounds like 'surplus'.\n\nAfter dinner, families watch the Spring Festival Gala on TV. At midnight, people set off fireworks to welcome the new year. Children are very happy because they can get red envelopes with money inside.\n\nDuring Spring Festival, people visit their relatives and friends. They say 'Happy New Year' to each other. It is a time for family, love, and hope for the future.",
